body.p:
The Office objects to FIG. 5C under 37 C.F.R. § 1.84(p)(4) for "includ[ing] two labels 74a and two labels 74b designating different areas of the brainstem." Action at 2. That is not so. "FIG. 5C shows 3D representations of the sections of FIGs. 5A and 5B at the first and second times (solid and mesh, respectively) superimposed on one another." Specification atSVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1470.08[0028] (emphasis added). Thus, FIG. 5C shows 3D representation 74a of a section of thecentral nervous system at a first time and 3D representation 74b of the same section of the central nervous system at a second time superimposed on one another. See id. at    [0027]- [0028], [0047], [0063], FIGs. 5A-5C. The multiple 74a's and multiple 74b's in FIG. 5C are not used to designate different parts of the brainstem but instead serve to help delineate where the first 3D representation (74a, solid) is and where the second 3D representation (74b, mesh) is. See id. Applicant respectfully requests reconsideration and withdrawal of the objection. III.   Claim Objections
